<title>GERMANY: Volkswagen denies plans new Polish plants.</title>
<headline>Volkswagen denies plans new Polish plants.</headline>
<dateline>BREMEN, Germany 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volkswagen AG on Tuesday denied reports from the Polish news agency PAP that it is planning to build new car plants in Jelenia Gora in Poland.</p>
<p>&quot;I do not know anything about that, I cannot confirm the story,&quot; a spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Volkswagen holds 59 percent of a production plant in Poznan, where 7,500 Transporter vans and 15,000 Skodas are produced annually.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
